# Component Structure Rules

## File Organization
- Keep components small and focused (max 200 lines)
- Extract custom hooks for reusable logic
- Use barrel exports (`index.ts`) for clean imports
- Group related files in folders

## Component Structure
```typescript
// 1. Imports
import React, { useState, useEffect, useCallback } from 'react';
import { Pokemon } from '@/shared/types';
import { getPokemonDetails } from '@/shared/api';

// 2. Types/Interfaces
interface PokemonCardProps {
  pokemon: Pokemon;
  onSelect?: (pokemon: Pokemon) => void;
}

// 3. Component
export const PokemonCard: React.FC<PokemonCardProps> = ({ 
  pokemon, 
  onSelect 
}) => {
  // 4. State
  const [isHovered, setIsHovered] = useState(false);
  
  // 5. Effects
  useEffect(() => {
    // Side effects
  }, []);
  
  // 6. Event handlers
  const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
    onSelect?.(pokemon);
  }, [pokemon, onSelect]);
  
  // 7. Render
  return (
    <div onClick={handleClick}>
      {/* JSX content */}
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Custom Hooks
```typescript
// hooks/usePokemonData.ts
export const usePokemonData = (id: string) => {
  const [pokemon, setPokemon] = useState<Pokemon | null>(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchPokemon = async () => {
      try {
        setLoading(true);
        const data = await getPokemonDetails(id);
        setPokemon(data);
      } catch (err) {
        setError('Failed to fetch Pokemon');
      } finally {
        setLoading(false);
      }
    };

    fetchPokemon();
  }, [id]);

  return { pokemon, loading, error };
};
```

## Barrel Exports
```typescript
// entities/pokemon/index.ts
export { PokemonCard } from './ui/PokemonCard';
export { PokemonType } from './ui/PokemonType';
export { PokemonStat } from './ui/PokemonStat';
export type { Pokemon, PokemonType as PokemonTypeData } from './types';
```

## Folder Structure
```
entities/pokemon/
├── ui/
│   ├── PokemonCard.tsx
│   ├── PokemonCard.stories.tsx
│   └── PokemonType.tsx
├── types/
│   └── index.ts
└── index.ts
```

## Naming Conventions
- Components: PascalCase (`PokemonCard`)
- Hooks: camelCase starting with `use` (`usePokemonData`)
- Files: PascalCase for components, camelCase for utilities
- Folders: kebab-case (`pokemon-detail`)

## Avoid
- Don't create overly complex components
- Don't mix UI and business logic
- Don't forget to export from index files
- Don't create deep folder nesting